+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`
+  - `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate`. It used `unit_price * rate`, so quantity was ignored (PRICING.md rule 3).
+  - `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for a rate name not in `RATES` (rule 3). Before, a bad rate only failed later, at `vat` time, with a `KeyError`.
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: corrected `test_reduced_rate_small_item`. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52. Rule 4 says 0.50 × 0.05 = 0.025 rounds half up to 0.03, so the test now expects VAT 0.03 and gross 0.53. I judged the old test wrong, not the code.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` before the change: 4 of 6 tests failed.
+- `python -m unittest` after the change: 6 tests ran, all OK.
+- I worked out the expected values in the other tests by hand against PRICING.md. They match: 2.994 → 2.99, and 5.00 + 0.16 = 5.16.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- No other tests or callers exist beyond `tests/test_invoice.py`. I did not check anything outside this repo.
+- Nothing outside `billing/`, `tests/` and `SUMMARY.md` needed changes. `docs/PRICING.md` is untouched.
